    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03142": {
      "title": "Junior Specialist",
      "description": "Junior Specialist - Szumlinski Laboratory, Department of Psychological & Brain Sciences (JPF03142) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Junior Specialist - Szumlinski Laboratory, Department of Psychological & Brain Sciences (JPF03142) Junior Specialist - Szumlinski Laboratory, Department of Psychological & Brain Sciences Apply now to Junior Specialist - Szumlinski Laboratory, Department of Psychological & Brain Sciences Job #JPF03142 Psychological and Brain Sciences / College of Letters & Science - Mathematical, Life, and Physical Sciences / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Salary range: A reasonable estimate that the University expects to pay for this position at 100% is $58,300 to $72,500 annually. Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: September 2026 or later Position duration: This will be a one-year position with a comprehensive benefits package with the possibility of renewal. Continuation beyond one year will be based on performance and availability of funding. Application Window Open date: August 31, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Sep 14, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Junior Specialist will participate fully in neuroscience and behavior research focused on the biobehavioral consequences of repeated stimulant and alcohol exposure. The position involves assisting with study design and performing rat and mouse behavioral studies of drug self-administration, cognition, and anxiety. Will also perform immunoblotting and immunohistochemical procedures to include image analysis. Assisting with training undergraduate student RAs, data management, statistical analysis, assisting the PI and research team with presentations at lab meetings and at psychology and neuroscience conferences, and authorship on academic research articles. Additional duties will include:  managing IACUC protocols and reviews and maintaining/ordering lab supplies to ensure all research projects are executed properly. The Junior Specialist will also engage in specialized research, professional activity, and University and/or public service. Specialists use their professional expertise to make scientific and scholarly contributions to the research enterprise of the University and to achieve recognition in the professional and scientific community. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must have completed or be currently enrolled in a Bachelor's degree in Psychology, Neuroscience or a related field at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) -Applicants currently enrolled in a BA or BS program, must have a bachelor’s degree conferred by the start date of the position -At least 12 months of experience working in a research setting with rats and/or mice as research subjects. Preferred qualifications -Experience in standard laboratory techniques, including immunoblotting and/or immunohistochemistry. -Candidates must be able to work both independently and in collaboration with others, have strong multi-tasking, problem-solving, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Applicants that are chosen for an interview will have their references contacted after the interview. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03142 Help contact: pamelawilks@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining 