    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03131": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Business EthicsApply nowto Lecturer in Business Ethics",
      "description": "Lecturer in Business Ethics (JPF03131) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturer in Business Ethics (JPF03131) Lecturer in Business Ethics Apply now to Lecturer in Business Ethics Job #JPF03131 Religious Studies / College of Letters & Science - Humanities and Fine Arts / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Lecturer Salary range: A reasonable estimated full-time rate for this position at 100% time is $73,817 to $78,314 annually. Percent appointments may vary.  See Table 15 for the salary range. See Table 15 for the salary range. Percent time: 33% Anticipated start: 1/4/2027 for Winter Quarter and 3/29/2027 for Spring Quarter. Position duration: 1 Quarter Application Window Open date: September 24, 2026 Next review date: Thursday, Oct 8, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Walter H. Capps Center for the Study of Ethics, Religion, and Public Life and the Department of Religious Studies at the University of California, Santa Barbara, is seeking to appoint an in-person, part-time Lecturer in Business Ethics to teach one course during the academic year 2026-2027. The candidate will be expected to teach a total of one course, an upper-division undergraduate class on “Business and Corporate Ethics,” during the Fall, Winter, or Spring term. The course will be concerned with instruction in the historic values and ethical principles of both Western and non-Western civilizations, and how these foundational principles bear upon responsible decision-making in a global world. Drawing upon the liberal arts tradition, the course will introduce students to diverse thinking on ethics, and how these principles can apply to complex decision making. Exposure to these modes of reflection will enhance ethical sensibility and provide an intellectual basis for addressing specific issues that CEOs and managers inevitably face. Inquiries may be directed to the department’s Academic Personnel Coordinator, through the help contact below. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) An MA, MBA, JD, or PhD in Business Administration, Economics, Philosophy, or Religious Studies, or Similar Degree in a Related Field, is required by time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Applicants who have 1 year or more of teaching experience. Applicants who have 3 years or more of professional experience in business or finance. Preferred qualifications Applicants who have academic degrees and experience in the Humanities and in Business. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Sample Syllabus Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) References may be contacted for candidates who advance as finalists. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03131 Help contact: amandalizarraga@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Lecturer in Business Ethics or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
