    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03162": {
      "title": "UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II",
      "description": "UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II - Director of Business Development (JPF03162) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II - Director of Business Development (JPF03162) UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II - Director of Business Development Apply now to UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II - Director of Business Development Job #JPF03162 Extension / Office of the Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Director of Business Development Salary range: $87,616- $121,675/year Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: 11/1/26 or later Position duration: This position goes through June 30, 2028 and may be renewable. Application Window Open date: October 13, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Oct 27, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Thursday, Dec 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description UC Santa Barbara Professional and Continuing Education (PaCE) integrates UC academic excellence with practical, career-relevant education in Southern California. PaCE programs provide the local workforce with skills to advance careers. A core goal is to work synergistically with local government and companies to enhance employee productivity and competitiveness. In this context, the Director of Business Development provides strategic leadership for UCSB Professional and Continuing Education (PaCE) by developing and implementing growth strategies aligned with institutional priorities and workforce market demands. In partnership with PaCE leadership, the incumbent identifies opportunities for new programs, advises on market positioning, and strengthens the university’s presence through collaboration with workforce boards, government agencies, economic development groups, industry organizations, and community partners. The position also serves as a key representative of PaCE, cultivating relationships that expand partnerships and enhance institutional visibility. Further, this role is responsible for driving revenue generation through the identification and development of corporate education contracts, customized training programs, grants, and strategic partnerships. The Director leads proposal development, negotiates agreements, oversees sales and pipeline management processes, and works collaboratively with internal teams to ensure responsive, high-quality program delivery. The position also supports grant-funded workforce initiatives through proposal writing, budget coordination, and stakeholder engagement. Finally, the incumbent collaborates across academic, marketing, outreach, and customer success teams to ensure operational effectiveness and program success. Responsibilities include establishing and monitoring key performance indicators, analyzing data to guide decision-making, and preparing reports for leadership on revenue growth, partnerships, and client outcomes Duties Include: Strategic Leadership & Planning, Partnership Development, and Institutional Collaboration Working independently, in collaboration with the Dean, Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, and the Chief Operating Officer, the Director of Business Development: Develops, implements, and evaluates a comprehensive business development strategy for UCSB Professional and Continuing Education (PaCE) aligned with institutional priorities and market opportunities. Provide high-level strategic counsel to the PaCE Dean and leadership team on growth initiatives and market positioning. Informs PaCE Leadership of opportunities and strategic choices to help direct the development of new programs. Leads and facilitates strategic planning processes that engage off-campus stakeholders to drive innovation and alignment. Represents PaCE across local and regional communities by cultivating strategic relationships with Workforce Development Boards, Chambers of Commerce, Economic Development Organizations, government agencies, industry associations, and other key partners to expand the university’s reach and develop B2B partnerships and business opportunities. Cultivates and maintains strong relationships with corporate, government, nonprofit, and industry leaders to establish and grow collaborative partnerships. Serves as the principal liaison for strategic external partners, ensuring consistent communication and mutual value creation. Represents PaCE at key professional and community events to elevate visibility and promote partnership opportunities. Revenue Generation & Sales Management Proactively researches, identifies, and pursues new revenue opportunities, including corporate education contracts, customized training programs, and strategic partnerships that align with institutional goals. Leads the development of compelling proposals and detailed project plans; negotiates terms and manages client relationships to ensure successful execution and achievement of revenue targets. Designs, implements, and oversees effective sales processes, including pipeline development, forecasting, and performance metrics to drive consistent growth and accountability. Works with the Manager of Customer Success and Outreach to develop best practices and response protocols to facilitate sales and interactions with corporate and government entities. Identifies and pursues grant-funded workforce development opportunities for PaCE at the local, regional, state, and federal levels. Collaborate with subject matter experts to develop program content and lead the proposal development process, including grant writing, budget creation, submission coordination, and related supporting documentation. Institutional Collaboration and Performance Management Collaborates with the Programs, Marketing, Customer Success, and Outreach teams to develop and execute integrated business strategies. Collaborates with cross-functional teams to ensure timely, market-responsive solutions and the successful delivery of customized education programs. Works with the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and Program Managers to direct and oversee the design and implementation of high-quality, tailored education offerings that meet client and market needs. Defines, monitors, and refines key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure success in revenue generation, partnership development, and client satisfaction. Conducts regular data analysis to guide strategic decision-making, optimize resource allocation, and inform program enhancements. Composes, prepares, and presents comprehensive reports to PaCE leadership, highlighting performance trends, actionable insights, and recommendations for sustained growth and innovation. Department : https://professional.ucsb.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Master’s degree in a related field Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in business development, sales pipeline management, or strategic partnership cultivation within higher education, corporate learning and development (L&D), or workforce development. Minimum of 3 years of experience in strategic planning and managing complex, service-driven programs within an academic environment, including direct responsibility for developing or expanding self-supporting, tuition-driven, or continuing education offerings. Preferred qualifications Experience leading the development of business proposals, grant applications, and project plans, including contract negotiation and grant administration or Principal Investigator (PI)-level leadership. Knowledge of business culture, strategic thinking, intercultural communication, risk assessment, and program management. Proven ability to build relationships and work effectively across divisions; Excellent problem-solving, negotiation, and oral/written communication skills. Expertise in designing, implementing, and overseeing effective sales processes, including pipeline development, forecasting, and performance metrics. Demonstrated ability to define Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and utilize data analysis to guide strategic decision-making and reporting. Proven track record of proactively generating revenue by researching, identifying, and securing customized training programs and corporate education contracts. Experience cultivating strong partnerships and serving as a principal liaison to corporate, government, nonprofit, and industry leaders. Familiarity with local and regional workforce development organizations, partnerships, and funding ecosystems. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Reference requirements 2-4 required (contact information only) The department will conduct a reference check for the finalist before extending an offer. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03162 Help contact: julia.choi@professional.ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to UCSB PaCE Academic Coordinator II - Director of Business Development or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03168": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI (JPF03168)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI (JPF03168) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI (JPF03168) Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI Apply now to Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI Job #JPF03168 Film and Media Studies / College of Letters & Science - Humanities and Fine Arts / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Assistant Professor Salary range: $88,300-$114,400 Percent time: 100% FTE Anticipated start: July 1, 2027 or later Application Window Open date: October 6, 2026 Next review date: Friday, Nov 6, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Film and Media Studies at UC Santa Barbara invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Media Industries and AI. We seek a scholar whose research and teaching examines artificial intelligence as a media industry phenomenon, including its infrastructures, labor, political economy, regulation, and cultural, artistic, and social implications. We welcome candidates working on any global region and through any critical, historical, or empirical methodology, including but not limited to production studies, platform and infrastructure studies, science and technology studies, critical algorithm studies, political economy, labor studies, cultural and industrial history, and creative or practice-based research on generative media. We are especially interested in candidates who can speak to one or more of the following: the restructuring of film, television, gaming, digital media, and/or music industries by AI systems; the labor of AI production, from data annotation to creative and technical work displaced or transformed by automation; the environmental, material, and geopolitical infrastructures underlying AI; algorithmic culture, recommendation systems, and platform governance; or the aesthetics, authorship, and cultural politics of generative and synthetic media. This position calls for a humanities-based, critical, media industries approach to the study of AI—one attentive to history, culture, power, embodiment, and meaning-making, rather than a purely technical or computational orientation. We therefore welcome scholars whose work engages AI and media industries through racial, gender, queer, global and/or transnational, environmental, creative, and other critical approaches. Candidates for the position will be expected to teach in our core Film and Media Studies undergraduate and graduate curriculum, and to develop new courses—large lecture classes and smaller seminars—in their areas of expertise. They ideally will participate in existing research clusters and centers within our department, including the Carsey-Wolf Center and its Media Industries and AI Research Initiative, the Global Media Technologies and Cultures Lab, and Wireframe Studio, as well as those associated with other departments, programs, and centers on campus. The faculty of the Department of Film and Media Studies engages in scholarship and pedagogy across multiple scholarly approaches, fostering a dynamic and expansive understanding of film and media study. We are a robust department with over 500 undergraduate majors and 30 doctoral students. With this appointment, we seek to extend the department’s scholarly and curricular strengths and advance our department’s commitment to diverse, interdisciplinary research and teaching. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) The minimum qualification to be considered for this position is the completion of all requirements for a PhD except the dissertation in Film and Media Studies or a related discipline at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Evidence of an active research agenda Completion of PhD by appointment start date Preferred qualifications Teaching experience at the university or college level defined as a minimum of one year as teaching assistant or instructor of record Evidence of a strong commitment to teaching as indicated by syllabi, teaching evaluations, reference letters, or candidate teaching statement Record of peer-reviewed publications Demonstrated interest in and use of innovative teaching methods and tools Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Letter of Application -   Two pages outlining the candidate's research, teaching, and service experience and their qualifications for the position. Statement of Research -   Two pages describing the applicant's current and future research program in media industries and AI, situating their work within film and media studies, articulating a clear trajectory for future scholarship. Statement of Teaching -   Two pages addressing teaching qualifications, pedagogical approaches, and potential contributions to the teaching culture of the department. Sample Syllabus #1 -   A sample syllabus for a large lecture course Sample Syllabus #2 -   A sample syllabus for a small seminar course Teaching Evaluations -   Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness - These might include course evaluation scores, student narrative evaluation of teaching performance, and/or peer or supervisor observation. (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 letters of reference required We must receive letters from a minimum of 3 references. Applicants must request letters of reference through the UC Recruit system in order to complete their application. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03168 Help contact: savannah@filmandmedia.ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor in Media Industries and AI or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03171": {
      "title": "UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor",
      "description": "UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor - UX/UI Design (JPF03171) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor - UX/UI Design (JPF03171) UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor - UX/UI Design Apply now to UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor - UX/UI Design Job #JPF03171 Extension / Office of the Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Salary range: A reasonable estimate for this position is $2,000.00–$4,250.00 per course. Application Window Open date: October 13, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Oct 27, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Mar 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description We are looking for an instructor who can create a studio environment where students learn by doing. Students will conduct research, develop concepts, build prototypes, test their ideas, respond to critique, and communicate their work. This is not a traditional lecture-based UX/UI course. The instructor should be comfortable helping students navigate ambiguity rather than simply teaching a prescribed software workflow. The program emphasizes curiosity, evidence, experimentation, iteration, and the ability to identify opportunities that may not initially be obvious. By the end of the sequence, students will have developed a body of work including research, experience maps, UX/UI concepts, Figma prototypes, usability testing evidence, MVP work, and portfolio quality case studies. Applicants should indicate areas of expertise such as front-end development, JavaScript programming, UI/UX design, or responsive web architecture. Instructor duties include but are not limited to: Design course structure, including modules, lessons, and learning objectives Develop and refine instructional materials for online delivery, including video-based lessons, slides, and supporting content Develop hands-on coding projects and assessments aligned with course outcomes and real-world use cases Create engaging learning activities that support applied skill development Update course content periodically to reflect current web standards, tools, and professional practices Communicate learning objectives, course expectations, and grading policies clearly Respond to student questions and learning needs in a timely and professional manner Evaluate student performance and assign grades based on established learning outcomes Submit final grades within university timelines and maintain appropriate student records in accordance with University policies The posting will remain open until March 31, 2027 to accommodate department needs. The pool will close on March 31, 2027; if you would like to continue to be considered after that time, and the pooled position is advertised again, you will need to submit a new application. Please note: The use of an instructor pool does not guarantee that an open position exists at the time you are applying. See the review date specified in UC Recruit to learn whether the department is currently reviewing applications for an upcoming opening. If there is no future review date specified, your application may not be considered at this time. Screening of applicants begins immediately after the Initial Review Date has passed; some appointments may begin as early as the 2027 Winter quarter. The number of these temporary, part-time, non-tenure track, academic positions varies from quarter to quarter, depending on the needs of the department. Appointments are offered on a course-by-course basis, and appointment length is based upon course section schedule(s). Appointments may be renewable based on need, funding, and performance. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) A bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Web Development, Design, or a related discipline OR 4 years of experience in web development, software engineering, or UX/UI. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Minimum of 3 years of professional experience in UI/UX design, or related design experience. Professional UX/UI portfolio. Preferred qualifications 5+ years of professional experience in UX/UI design. Experience with Figma. Experience conducting qualitative research and usability testing. Experience mentoring junior designers or students. Experience working on digital products or services from concept through testing. Experience incorporating AI tools into contemporary design workflows. Experience collaborating with external clients, stakeholders, or organizations. Experience with user-centered design and research. Graduate degree in UX, HCI, design, interaction design, human-centered design, or a related field is welcome but not required. The ability to explain complex design concepts clearly to students with different academic and professional backgrounds. Application Requirements Document requirements Applicants should indicate their areas of professional expertise (e.g., front-end development, JavaScript, UI/UX design, or related areas). In the cover letter, please describe the specific course topics or subject areas you are most qualified to teach and/or develop. Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Teaching (Optional) UX/UI Portfolio Reference requirements 2-4 required (contact information only) The department will conduct a reference check for the finalist before extending an offer. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03171 Help contact: julia.choi@professional.ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to UCSB PaCE Part-Time Instructor - UX/UI Design or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
