    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03173": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface, UC Santa Barbara (JPF03173) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface, UC Santa Barbara (JPF03173) Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface, UC Santa Barbara Apply now to Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface, UC Santa Barbara Job #JPF03173 Marine Science Institute / Office of Research / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface Salary range: A reasonable estimate for this position at 100% time is $71,491 to $85,736. Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: Start date is negotiable and is anticipated sometime in Summer or Fall 2027 Application Window Open date: October 16, 2026 Next review date: Wednesday, Dec 2, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Friday, Apr 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The University of California, Santa Barbara seeks a highly motivated postdoctoral scholar to lead a new research program examining how wildlife communities respond to the rapidly expanding wildland-urban interface. As development increasingly borders and fragments natural habitat, an important set of ecological and conservation questions is emerging: How do animal communities change across the transition from relatively intact wildlands to developed landscapes? Which species tolerate or exploit edges, and which are displaced by them? Do protected lands adjacent to development function as refuges, foraging habitat, or movement corridors? How do human-associated resources alter wildlife behavior and food webs? Can strategically-protected habitat at the wildland-urban boundary help sustain ecological communities while reducing negative interactions between wildlife and people? This research will address these questions in the Santa Barbara foothills surrounding Los Padres National Forest, an area of mountain wildlands abutting developed coastal landscapes. Specific research questions will be developed collaboratively with the successful candidate, who will have substantial intellectual freedom to shape the scientific direction of the project. Example research questions may include: ● How do vertebrate species richness, community composition, and activity change across gradients of human development? ● Which species are most sensitive to wildland-urban edges, and which species benefit from or tolerate them? ● Does wildlife activity become increasingly nocturnal near residences and other human activity? ● How do responses to development differ among mammals, birds, bats, amphibians, and other vertebrate groups? ● How do wildlife responses to developed edges change seasonally or during periods of drought and resource limitation? ● Do protected areas at the wildland-urban boundary function primarily as habitat, refuge, foraging areas, or movement corridors? ● How does proximity to development alter wildlife diets and trophic interactions? ● When and why do wildlife begin relying on human-associated foods, ornamental vegetation, commensal prey, or other anthropogenic resources? ● More broadly, what characteristics make protected lands at the wildland-urban interface most effective at maintaining biodiversity and ecological function? The project will be designed to integrate multiple complementary approaches. Specific methodologies will be shaped collaboratively with the successful candidate based on their expertise and research interests and may include: ● deployment and analysis of a camera-trap array ● standardized wildlife scat surveys ● environmental and scat DNA approaches ● non-invasive genetic identification and genotyping of focal wildlife species ● dietary DNA metabarcoding ● passive acoustic monitoring of birds, bats, amphibians, and other vocal taxa ● automated/AI-assisted classification of camera and acoustic data ● spatial analyses of wildlife occurrence and activity ● quantitative analysis of biodiversity, activity, behavior, diet, and community composition ● integration of field, molecular, and environmental datasets The successful candidate will be encouraged to develop additional questions that take advantage of this study system and to use the resulting datasets as a foundation for independent publications and external funding proposals. The postdoctoral scholar will take the lead in developing field and analytical research plans; managing research logistics; coordinating field sampling; collecting, managing, and analyzing data; working with collaborators conducting molecular and other specialized analyses; preparing peer-reviewed publications; presenting results at scientific conferences; and communicating findings to relevant stakeholders and the broader community. Additional funding is available to support these related research questions. The project will also establish a rigorous ecological baseline for long-term monitoring or impact studies. This will allow future studies to quantify wildlife responses to wildfire, drought, vegetation change, restoration, invasive-species management, or other environmental disturbances rather than attempting to reconstruct ecological conditions retrospectively. The postdoc will work closely with Professors at UC Santa Barbara, along with additional UCSB researchers and project collaborators. The position will be based at UC Santa Barbara, with regular field work in the Santa Barbara foothills. This position is fully funded for two years by the UCSB Schmidt Environmental Solutions Program. Department : https://msi.ucsb.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must have completed all requirements for a Ph.D. program (or equivalent), except the dissertation, in ecology, wildlife biology, conservation biology, environmental science, or a related field at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Applicants must have a doctoral degree in ecology, wildlife biology, conservation biology, environmental science, or a related field by the time of appointment. Preferred qualifications We are seeking candidates with a strong background in field ecology, wildlife ecology, conservation biology, community ecology, spatial ecology, molecular ecology, or related areas. Depending on the candidate's expertise and anticipated research questions, particularly useful experience may include: ● wildlife camera trapping or other automated biodiversity monitoring ● vertebrate field ecology, particularly mammalian ecology ● eDNA, non-invasive genetics, DNA metabarcoding, or molecular ecology ● acoustic biodiversity monitoring ● spatial ecology, GIS, occupancy modeling, movement ecology, or spatial statistics ● analysis of large camera-trap, acoustic, genomic, or other ecological datasets ● statistical approaches appropriate for replicated field datasets, including hierarchical, mixed-effects, or Bayesian models ● reproducible data management and analysis in R, Python, or comparable platforms Candidates are not expected to have expertise in all of these approaches. We are particularly interested in scientists who bring deep expertise in one or more areas and are excited about integrating their work with complementary field, molecular, and analytical approaches. The ideal candidate will also: ● take a rigorous and creative approach to ecological research ● have a strong record of scientific presentations and peer-reviewed publication appropriate to career stage ● have a demonstrated history of effective communication with principal investigators, research partners, students, land managers, and other stakeholders ● be enthusiastic about developing independent research questions within a collaborative project ● be comfortable leading field research and coordinating field and laboratory workflows ● have strong organizational and time-management skills ● be a respectful, professional, reliable, and collaborative colleague ● have an interest in connecting fundamental ecological questions with applied biodiversity conservation Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter -   Please describe your research background, relevant experience, and interest in the position. We particularly encourage applicants to briefly describe questions they might be interested in pursuing related to wildlife ecology at the wildland-urban interface and how their expertise could complement the broader project. Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) The search committee will contact references of the top candidate(s) after the interviews. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03173 Help contact: lswanson@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA UCSB Apply now to Postdoctoral Researcher in Wildlife Ecology at the Wildland-Urban Interface, UC Santa Barbara or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03174": {
      "title": "Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03174)",
      "description": "Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03174) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03174) Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute Apply now to Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute Job #JPF03174 California NanoSystems Institute / Office of Research / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Salary range: A reasonable estimate that the University expects to pay for this position at 100% time is $84,000-$150,000. Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: November 2026 or later Position duration: One year appointment, with the possiblity of renewal Application Window Open date: October 22, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Nov 9, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Sunday, Feb 28, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The NSF ExFAB BioFoundry (“ExFAB”) is user facility dedicated to developing and applying novel automated workflows to learn, prototype, and translate biology from unusual microbes into new biotechnologies. ExFAB’s focus is on the microbes that do not conform to standard growth habits and culture conditions or defy our current understanding of biology yet possess traits (e.g. pathways, proteins and structures) that biotechnology should harness. The ExFAB facilities span three campuses: UC Santa Barbara, UC Riverside and Cal Poly Pomona. The UCSB facility features a first of-its-kind anaerobic chamber. The ExFAB Automation Specialist is responsible for collaborating with ExFAB facility users (including both internal and external academics, as well as industry and national laboratories) in developing and performing research experiments that leverage ExFAB’s automated systems – from bioprospecting new functions to realizing microbial synthetic biology. In particular, the Automation Specialist will interface with users and lead all aspects of programming, testing, and optimizing ExFAB’s integrated automation platforms, many of which are contained in an anaerobic enclosure. It is expected that substantive scientific scholarly papers and conference presentations regularly result from these collaborations, as well as novel workflows for manipulating microbes and microbial communities. This will further result in published protocols and workflows that can be utilized by the broader microbiology research community. The ExFAB Automation Specialist is expected to represent ExFAB at relevant academic conferences and to identify and seek supplemental extramural funding, as appropriate. This role involves managing platforms and instrumentation for growth, phenotyping, nucleic assay preparation, and microbial transformation. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Biological Sciences, Chemical Engineering, Bioengineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a related field, with 3–5 years of relevant experience; or a Master’s degree in a relevant field with 1+ year of relevant experience (automation,  computation, etc.). Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Computation experience (coding, editing existing code) Experience in developing automation workflows that recapitulate wet-lab experiments (for biology or otherwise) Employment at the Associate Specialist level may be considered for applicants with a Master's degree or with at least 5 years of experience in  Computer Science, Biological Sciences, Chemical Engineering, Bioengineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a related field. Employment at the Full Specialist level may be considered for applicants with a PhD or with at least 10 years of experience in  Computer Science, Biological Sciences, Chemical Engineering, Bioengineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a related field. Preferred qualifications Basic knowledge of cell biology and biomolecular characterization techniques Strong understanding of biology and microbiology, including proteomics, metabolomics, phenotyping and genetics Demonstrated communication and organization skills to prioritize coordination of multiple assignments/projects/deadlines simultaneously with minimal direction Evidence of flexibility and initiative when working within a fast-paced, changing environment Management of multiple projects in both team-oriented collaborations and independent ownership Familiarity with Laboratory Information Management Systems (LIMS) Excellent written communication skills Master’s or PhD Degree in related field. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research -   Please include relevant experience with automation and computational (coding, editing of existing code, etc.) experience. Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) References will be checked after interviews for the top two candidates. We will contact you before we reach out to references. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03174 Help contact: alexis_torres@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Automation Specialists, ExFAB BioFoundry (2 Positions) in the California NanoSystems Institute or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03175": {
      "title": "Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03175)",
      "description": "Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03175) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute (JPF03175) Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute Apply now to Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute Job #JPF03175 California NanoSystems Institute / Office of Research / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Salary range: A reasonable estimate that the University expects to pay this position at 100% time is $120,000-$145,000. Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: January 4th, 2027 Position duration: One year appointment, with the possiblity of renewal Application Window Open date: October 23, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Nov 16, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Sunday, Jan 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The NSF ExFAB Biofoundry (“ExFAB”) is user facility dedicated to developing and applying novel automated workflows to learn, prototype, and translate biology from unusual microbes into new biotechnologies. ExFAB’s focus is on the microbes that do not conform to standard growth habits and culture conditions or defy our current understanding of biology yet possess traits (e.g. pathways, proteins and structures) that biotechnology should harness. The ExFAB facilities span three campuses: UC Santa Barbara, UC Riverside and Cal Poly Pomona. The UCSB facility features a first-of-its-kind anaerobic chamber. The primary focus of the ExFAB Computation and Data Specialist is to provide data analysis, data infrastructure, development of AI-based model training and AI-readiness of datasets. The position supports the DTBL (Design-Test-Build-Learn) Cycle, including management of the massive datasets generated by the ExFAB user facility, enabling efficient data exploration and interpretation by users and by AI agents, and providing project tracking. Responsibilities include: Pipeline Development. The ExFAB Computation and Data Specialist provides support to develop workflows across the biofoundry for data acquisition and analysis for AI-readiness, processing and analysis across data modalities including but not limited to imaging, flow cytometry, metabolomics, and associated metadata. This includes building flexible analysis pipelines, creating machine learning models to maximize the utility of generated data, helping push data exploration and managing data storage systems. Data Analysis Support. The ExFAB Computation and Data Specialist works closely with domain scientists across the biofoundry to develop customized analysis approaches tailored to non-standard biology, including customized advanced imaging processing (filtering, thresholding, segmentation. Object detection, and tracking for time-series or live imaging, handling high-dimensional datasets flow cytometry) and integration across modalities. Also supports the develop of quantitative data analysis workflows and statistically robust outputs. Data Infrastructure and Support. The ExFAB Computation and Data Specialist establish systems for data organization, storage, and linkage across experiments and modalities across the biofoundry. Provides dedicated management for the UCSB ExFAB team’s LIMS (Laboratory Information Management System) engagement, including training, troubleshooting, and collaboration with the UCR LIMS team. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Master’s Degree in biological science or engineering, including Computer Science, with an emphasis on data and computation or at least 5 years of experience demonstrating expertise in creating and/or administering scientific data organization and/or data mining structures, at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) Employment at the Full Specialist level may be considered for applicants with a PhD or with at least 10 years of experience in Computer Science, Biological Sciences, Chemical Engineering, Bioengineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a related field. Preferred qualifications • Experience working with microbiology, including proteomics, metabolomics, phenotyping and genetic engineering • Multiple programming language (Python, R and/or SQL) • Demonstrated communication and organization skills to prioritize coordination of multiple assignments/projects/deadlines simultaneously with minimal direction • Evidence of flexibility and initiative when working within a fast-paced, changing environment • Management of multiple projects in both team-oriented collaborations and independent ownership • Familiarity with Laboratory Information Management Systems (LIMS) • Excellent written communication skills • PhD Degree in related field. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) References will be checked after interviews for the top two candidates. We will contact you before we reach out to references Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03175 Help contact: alexis_torres@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Computation and Data Specialist, ExFAB BioFoundry in the California NanoSystems Institute or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03176": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) (JPF03176)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) (JPF03176) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) (JPF03176) Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) Apply now to Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) Job #JPF03176 California NanoSystems Institute / Office of Research / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Postdoctoral Researcher-- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome Salary range: $71,491-$85,736 annually Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: 11/30/26 or later Position duration: Two years, with the possibility of extension. Application Window Open date: October 26, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Nov 9, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Friday, Jan 8, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The University of California, Santa Barbara (UCSB) California NanoSystems Institute (CNSI) invites applications for two (2) Postdoctoral Research positions in machine learning and computational modeling, focused on identifying pathways involving the gut-brain axis that link the infant microbiome with neurodevelopment and Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD). This project is part of the Wellcome Leap FORM initiative: Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (Wellcome Leap Form) and involves closed-loop collaborations between experiments, modeling, and lived experiences (Wellcome Leap Awards). Statistical and dynamical models will be developed based on metabolomic and metagenomic data obtained from experiments conducted in UCSB’s ExFAB BioFoundry for Extreme and Exceptional Fungi, Archea, and Bacteria (ExFAB website) in parallel with the modeling effort. Perturbation, dynamic trajectory, stability, and resilience analysis will follow a closed-loop format linking AI and dynamical models with experimental protocols and outcomes. The successful candidate will contribute to this work with freedom to pursue creative interests related to the project. They will have access to the broad multidisciplinary research environment at UCSB, including the REAL AI initiative, which focuses on developing AI-powered digital twins for complex systems, the Departments of Physics, Ecology, Evolution and Marine Biology, Psychology and Brain Sciences, the College of Engineering, and the Koegel Autism Center. Link to REAL Al website. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must have completed all requirements for a  PhD (or equivalent) in Physics, Computer Science, Bioengineering, Ecology, or a related field, except the dissertation, at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) PhD in Physics, Computer Science, Bioengineering, Ecology, or a related field  required at the time of appointment. Preferred qualifications ● Coding fluency in Python for machine learning and statistical analyses. ● Excellent statistical and/or causal inference skills. ● Experience with modeling and statistical analysis of metagenomic and metabelomic data. ● Strong background in ecological theory and modeling. ● Experience leading peer-reviewed publications and/or reports. ● Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with an ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary team. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Applicants must provide the names and contact information of their references. The hiring unit will request confidential letters from the references of those applicants who are under serious consideration. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03176 Help contact: alexis_torres@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Postdoctoral Researcher -- Foundations of a Resilient Microbiome (2 Positions) or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03181": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes (JPF03181)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes (JPF03181) - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes (JPF03181) Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes Job #JPF03181 Earth Research Institute / Office of Research / UC Santa Barbara Position overview Position title: Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes Salary range: $71,491 - $82,677 Percent time: 100% Anticipated start: January 4, 2027 or later Position duration: 2 years Application Window Open date: October 22, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Nov 23, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Dec 16, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Applications are invited for a postdoctoral scholar to engage in research as part of a collaborative team across University of Utah, University of California Irvine, and University of California Santa Barbara focused on understanding disturbance impacts on terrestrial carbon cycling in the continental US and Canada. The postdoctoral scholar will lead work on developing and validating vegetation models for key disturbance processes representative of forest dynamics across the US and Canada as part of a cohort of four postdoctoral team members across institutions. The postdoc will be based in the Trugman Lab at UC Santa Barbara. We seek a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to work at the interface disturbance ecology, forest dynamics, and ecosystem modeling based in the Trugman Lab at UC Santa Barbara. The successful candidate will work closely with an interdisciplinary team of ecologists, modelers, and remote sensing scientists to integrate remote sensing products and existing datasets into a mechanistic modeling framework. The position offers substantial intellectual independence and opportunities to publish high-impact research addressing forest resilience, disturbance regimes, and climate change. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must hold a PhD or must have completed all requirements for a PhD program (or equivalent) in ecology, environmental science, forestry, Earth system science, or a closely related field, except the dissertation, at the time of application. Additional qualifications (required at time of start) -PhD in ecology, environmental science, forestry, Earth system science, or a closely related field (completed by start date) Preferred qualifications -Experience running land surface models or other formulations of process-based vegetation models and experience developing new model processes -Familiarity with western U.S. forest ecosystems -A track record of scholarship including talks and peer-reviewed publications appropriate to career stage involving physics-based vegetation models as a primary tool for scientific inquiry -Strong quantitative skills and experience with ecological or Earth system models -Proficiency in programming and data analysis (e.g., R, Python, C/C++, or similar) -Strong written and verbal communication skills Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research -   A short (1-2 page) statement of research experience and interests related to the project Publications -   PDFs of up to 3 representative publications (preprints acceptable/encouraged) (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Please provide the full names, emails and phone numbers (for a possible follow up with the reference provider) of 3-5 references who are prepared to provide letters of recommendation upon request. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.ucsb.edu/JPF03181 Help contact: janhunter@ucsb.edu About UC Santa Barbara As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, students and third parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Additionally, you will be required to comply with the University of California Policy on Vaccination Programs , as may be amended or revised from time to time.  Federal, state, or local public health directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Job location Santa Barbara, CA Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar in Forest Resilience to Climate Extremes or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California Santa Barbara is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California Santa Barbara is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California Santa Barbara Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
